@startuml Locator_Resolution

skinparam backgroundColor #FEFEFE
skinparam defaultFontSize 11
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam activityDiamondFontSize 11

<style>
' Named node styles instead of the deprecated "#RRGGBB:label;" colour prefix,
' which newer PlantUML rejects in favour of a trailing <<stereotype>>.
' This form renders on both old and new versions.
.found   { BackgroundColor #C8E6C9 }
.slm     { BackgroundColor #FFE0B2 }
.vlm     { BackgroundColor #BBDEFB }
.failure { BackgroundColor #FFCDD2 }
</style>

title Locating an element - resolution flow (ADR-022 / ADR-024)\nClick Visual  text=Save || desc="save button in the toolbar"

start
:locator string from the test;
if (a DOM is loaded?) then (no)
  :error: "No DOM loaded.\nCall 'Dump Visual DOM' first."; <<failure>>
  stop
else (yes)
endif

:split on "||" (quote-aware)
-> ordered ALTERNATIVES
each alternative = AND-group of locators
(id= text= hint= role= within= right_of= below= desc=);

while (next alternative?) is (yes)
  partition "Deterministic match  (ElementFinder)" #E8F5E9 {
    :match every locator in the group
    and INTERSECT the results;
    if (how many matched?) then (exactly 1)
      :element found; <<found>>
      detach
    elseif (several - AMBIGUOUS) then
      if (chain also has a desc= ?) then (yes)
        partition "Arbitration (ADR-024 v1.1)" #E3F2FD {
          :ground that description over
          JUST these candidates
          (2-3 elements = most reliable);
          if (confident?) then (yes)
            :element found\n(log: disambiguated to E48); <<vlm>>
            detach
          else (no)
          endif
        }
      else (no)
      endif
      :reason = "Multiple elements match";
    else (none)
      if (this alternative is a lone desc= ?) then (yes)
        partition "Tiered grounding (ADR-022)" #FFF3E0 {
          :DescriptionResolver.resolve()
          lexical -> SLM over DOM -> VLM Set-of-Mark
          (see the grounding diagram);
          if (a tier is confident?) then (yes)
            :element found\n(log: tier that answered); <<slm>>
            detach
          else (no)
          endif
        }
        :reason = "no grounding tier confident
        (nearest: ...)";
      else (no)
        :reason = "not found";
      endif
    endif
  }
  :record the attempt (rendered locator + reason)
  and fall through to the next alternative;
endwhile (no more)

:FAIL LOUDLY - every attempt reported:\nLocator did not resolve to exactly one element\ntried 1) text=Save    -> not found\n2) desc=...     -> no grounding tier confident; <<failure>>
stop

legend bottom
  **Exactly one, or fail.** An alternative is abandoned when it matches
  NOTHING *or* is AMBIGUOUS - clicking a coin-flip element is worse than
  failing. When a later alternative wins, a WARNING names the stale primary:
  the signal that feeds the planned self-healing locators.
  Existence checks (Visual Should Exist / Get Visual Elements) instead
  accept many matches, so there the first non-empty alternative wins.
end legend

@enduml
